Thank you, Ken.

45
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:21,640
Thank you to everyone at Canvas that has made this such a nice welcome,

46
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:24,780
starting with a lovely dinner last night.

47
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:28,240
I had a chance to meet the staff and some members of the board.

48
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:33,560
Thanks for being here and looking into this challenging book with me.

49
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:39,500
The approach that I am, I'll just put it this way, I'm from New Jersey, right?

50
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:50,220
So, the approach that I'm trying to sell is somewhat different from that which is most popularly known out there.

51
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:58,540
And if you take nothing away beside this, take this.

52
00:10:58,540 --> 00:11:05,680
There's value in reading Revelation alongside John's own congregations

53
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:13,020
and thinking with them about how they would have made sense of this word

54
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:18,600
because it unlocks challenges that Revelation poses to us

55
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:30,640
that we would tend to miss if we only approach Revelation the way the writers of books that actually sell

56
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:36,440
approach Revelation, namely as a roadmap for the end times,

57
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:43,080
whether that be the 19th century, the 20th century, or the 21st century,

58
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:47,000
they've been bestsellers in every one of those centuries.

59
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:55,800
Now, I have wrestled with Revelation, and in part, I've been in love with Revelation since I was 13 years old.

60
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,720
I was a strange kid.

61
00:11:57,720 --> 00:12:01,480
I'm a strange adult, let's be honest.

62
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:07,900
But I first read Revelation when I was 13 years of age, after I'd read through the Gospels and Acts.

63
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:11,020
Revelation was gripping.

64
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:20,480
Its fantastic and mysterious images, its cosmic scope, its astounding pronouncements about the stakes involved

65
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:24,240
in keeping or failing to keep its word.

66
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:30,420
Revelation was well-crafted to sink its hooks into the reader's mind.

67
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:39,020
As I sought guidance for understanding this word, and therefore having a chance at keeping this word,

68
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:46,200
I found that the people with whom I conversed about Revelation tended to have one of two reactions,

69
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:47,980
with very little in between.

70
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:54,640
The first is exemplified by the pastor of the Episcopal Church in which I was raised.

71
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:59,540
He was always open to discussing the faith and the Scriptures with me.

72
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:04,240
I found him to be a great encouragement throughout those teenage years.

73
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:08,380
But on this occasion, he admitted he had very little exposure to the book.

74
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:14,340
So he took me to the church library, sat me down with the last volume in the Old Interpreter's Bible,

75
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:15,820
and essentially wished me luck.

76
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:23,540
The second response is exemplified by my maternal grandmother's younger sister,

77
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,140
whom I simply called aunt.

78
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:30,380
Though raised Baptist, she had joined the Seventh-day Adventist Church.

79
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:34,280
And she knew exactly what Revelation was about from beginning to end.

80
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,520
She read about it constantly.

81
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:41,960
And my display of interest, which in retrospect was a bad choice on my part,

82
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:46,260
but my display of interest to her prompted a steady flow of conversation,

83
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:49,080
sharing of literature over the space of a decade.

84
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:54,500
In one setting, Revelation was beyond the purview of the professionals.

85
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:59,380
In the other setting, it was the interpretive key to the whole Bible,

86
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:03,480
the focus for study on the part of every active layperson.

87
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:09,060
In both settings, Revelation was a kind of Pandora's box.

88
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:12,520
In the first setting, the tendency was to keep a lid on it.

89
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:20,500
Maybe we'll take a few peeks at the redeemed in the New Jerusalem on All Saints' Day.

90
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:25,500
But for the most part, the contents of Revelation are kept safely locked away.

91
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:31,900
In the second setting, every church member becomes a Pandora,

92
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:37,680
eagerly throwing the box open and allowing its contents to overrun their world.

93
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:41,600
They chase the beast in this or that political figure.

94
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:44,300
They follow the whore to this or that country.

95
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:50,100
They see the gallop of the four horsemen in this or that series of news briefs.

96
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:56,960
Either way, I believe we lose the witness of John's voice in our churches.

97
00:14:56,960 --> 00:15:03,080
Where Revelation is not read or studied regularly, John simply remains mute.

98
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:08,240
Where Revelation is avidly consumed as a playbook for the end times,

99
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:11,240
John's voice in which the interpreters are always inevitably living,

100
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:14,940
John's voice also goes unheard.

101
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:22,660
This time, trumped by the interpreters who use Revelation to speak of things about which John never imagined.

102
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:28,440
In the process, the interpreters and their audiences lose sight of those things

103
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:33,440
that John did passionately seek to communicate to his churches.

104
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:40,180
As people get caught up in the imagery of Revelation and try to find answers to these questions,

105
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:46,040
they often fall headlong into what I would consider be some basic mistakes,

106
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:50,800
forgetting some of the most basic and important principles of studying the Bible.

107
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:58,100
In regard to Revelation, I find many popular speakers and writers and the many more who follow them

108
00:15:58,100 --> 00:16:05,460
who have been led astray by three basic fallacies, three myths, if you will, about Revelation.

109
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:07,520
And this is going to hurt.

110
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:13,300
Myth number one, Revelation is all about us.

111
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:20,520
We often forget, in our rush to turn to Scripture, to hear a word for us,

112
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:24,120
which is a good thing to do, but in our rush to do that,

113
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:29,680
we forget that all of these texts originally spoke a word for them,

114
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:36,080
for communities of faith removed from us by at least 19 centuries.

115
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:44,800
We are the secondary beneficiaries of the pastoral guidance initially intended for them.

116
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:51,500
John gives us some cues that should serve to remind us as attentive readers

117
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:56,740
that this book is not in the first instance about us.

118
00:16:56,740 --> 00:17:02,540
Specifically, John signals that Revelation is to be read as a letter.

119
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:06,740
After the introductory paragraphs, the first three verses,

120
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:09,460
in which John doesn't speak in his own voice,

121
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:12,260
but rather in an impersonal voice

122
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:16,820
that reminds us of the openings of certain books of the Hebrew prophets,

123
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:21,760
John's own voice sounds out in the fourth verse

124
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:25,280
in words that recall the opening of other early Christian letters.

125
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:28,600
John, to the seven churches that are in Asia,

126
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,580
grace to you and peace.

127
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:35,360
The standard formula with which ancient letters began,

128
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:39,860
sender to addressees, greetings, is clearly present.

129
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:44,980
John even uses that modification of the standard greeting

130
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:49,920
that is already familiar from early Christian letters written by Peter and Paul,

131
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:51,680
grace to you and peace.

132
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:55,400
This is a critically important reading cue.

133
00:17:57,580 --> 00:18:03,020
John is writing a letter addressed explicitly to seven real communities of Christians

134
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:06,560
in the Roman province of Asia, now in western Turkey.

135
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:11,760
This is reinforced by the divine command that John hears,

136
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:16,360
write down what you see into a scroll and send it to the seven churches,

137
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:21,960
to Ephesus and to Smyrna and to Pergamon and to Thyatira and to Sardis

138
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:24,820
and to Philadelphia and to Laodicea.

139
00:18:24,820 --> 00:18:31,760
This naturally implies that John intended his letter to be understood by them,

140
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:36,640
to shape their perceptions of their everyday realities,

141
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:41,840
and to motivate a particular response to their circumstances.

142
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:50,000
The pervasive use of the number seven in Revelation suggests that the seven churches are in some way

143
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,560
representative of the achievements and the challenges facing churches

144
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:59,740
across the Mediterranean in the first century and across the globe now,

145
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:04,700
such that the words addressed to them speak to churches beyond that circle.

146
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:12,740
Nevertheless, these seven churches are seven real churches facing particular difficulties and situations,

147
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:18,400
whose response to their world John wanted to affect profoundly.

148
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:25,600
A grounded and responsible reading of Revelation began disappointing with the second coming of Christ.

149
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:32,720
All three approaches are based on the assumption that by prophecy,

150
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:40,120
John primarily indicates that he is communicating predictions about specific events

151
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:45,140
that will yet unfold at some point in his first audience's future,

152
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,960
and that this is the interpretative key to the book.

153
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:52,560
They differ only in terms of the time frame of the fulfillment.

154
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:56,020
What is prophecy?

155
00:19:56,020 --> 00:20:01,920
This, the slides aren't changing on the screens.

156
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:10,680
Well, that's why there's a handout too.

157
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:18,260
Anyway, is prophecy essentially prediction?

158
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:21,740
If Revelation is a prophetic word,

159
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:28,060
does that mean it is a book of predictions that must be fulfilled at some point in history?

160
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,240
To answer this,

161
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:34,080
I'm just going to keep advancing my own slides because it makes me feel better.

162
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:35,840
To answer this,

163
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:39,620
I would turn to the prophetic utterances of the Hebrew Bible

164
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:43,920
and to the phenomenon of prophecy within the New Testament

165
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:46,020
and in early Christian worship.

166
00:20:46,940 --> 00:20:50,400
While such prophecy could include a predictive element,

167
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:54,220
it was also, and perhaps primarily,

168
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:57,600
a declaration of God's action in the present

169
00:20:57,600 --> 00:21:03,540
and an announcement of God's evaluation of the present actions of his people,

170
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:08,580
diagnosing problems, calling for realignment with God's values.

171
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:15,900
Prophecy is essentially a word from the Lord breaking into the situation of the Lord's people

172
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:21,220
who need guidance or encouragement or a call to repentance and recommitment.

173
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:28,820
Prophecy was also a regular experience in the worship life of the Pauline churches.

174
00:21:28,820 --> 00:21:33,400
The new pouring out of God's Holy Spirit on God's people

175
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:37,640
resulted in the renewed possibility of hearing God's voice

176
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:39,800
given utterance by the Spirit

177
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:43,140
through the mouths of those who were possessed by the Spirit.

178
00:21:44,140 --> 00:21:49,640
While there are certainly elements of prediction involved in some prophetic utterances,

179
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:52,360
such as we can find from Agabus in Acts,

180
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:56,360
the primary element appears to have been edification,

181
00:21:56,360 --> 00:22:00,320
the revelation of God's perspective

182
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:05,380
that invited a radical reorientation to one's circumstances,

183
00:22:05,380 --> 00:22:08,060
to one's practices, to one's pursuits.

184
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:11,360
This certainly emerges from Paul's own understanding

185
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:13,480
of what prophecy is for

186
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,720
when the prophetic gift is working at its best,

187
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:18,900
as we read in 1 Corinthians 14.

188
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:22,020
In John's own situation,

189
00:22:22,020 --> 00:22:25,580
Jezebel, I'm sure that's not her real name, right?

190
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:27,200
Who names her kid Jezebel?

191
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:32,440
But Jezebel's own activity as a prophet doesn't involve prediction.

192
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:34,400
It involves teaching

193
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:38,920
in regard to the boundaries of acceptable Christian practice,

194
00:22:38,920 --> 00:22:40,420
although in her case,

195
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:42,820
those boundaries are considerably wider

196
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:45,140
than John would understand them to be.

197
00:22:45,140 --> 00:22:47,420
In Revelation,

198
00:22:47,420 --> 00:22:51,780
what we typically call the seven letters to the seven churches

199
00:22:51,780 --> 00:22:54,020
are a prime example of,

200
00:22:54,020 --> 00:22:55,700
I would suggest they're better labeled,

201
00:22:55,700 --> 00:22:58,520
the seven oracles to the seven churches,

202
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:01,900
the seven prophetic words to the seven churches,

203
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:05,660
because after the command given to John to write down the oracle,

204
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:08,000
the actual message to each church

205
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:11,980
begins in a manner that recalls the prophetic formula,

206
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:14,320
thus says the Lord from the Old Testament.

207
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:15,020
For example,

208
00:23:15,020 --> 00:23:17,400
these are the words of the Son of God.

209
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:20,440
The risen and glorified Lord

210
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:22,460
speaks a word to the churches

211
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:24,380
through the prophet John,

212
00:23:24,380 --> 00:23:26,200
affirming their strengths,

213
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:28,320
diagnosing their weaknesses,

214
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:30,900
calling them to faithful action,

215
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:32,860
threatening judgment

216
00:23:32,860 --> 00:23:36,080
upon those who are recalcitrant

217
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:38,060
and promising favor

218
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:41,260
for those who are penitent and faithful.

219
00:23:41,260 --> 00:23:42,360
In short,

220
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:44,800
they do precisely what so much

221
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:47,820
of the prophetic writings of the Old Testament

222
00:23:47,820 --> 00:23:51,220
sought to do for the communities of Israel and Judah.

223
00:23:51,220 --> 00:23:55,580
Where a biblical prophet speaks about the future,

224
00:23:55,580 --> 00:23:57,900
he usually limits the prediction

225
00:23:57,900 --> 00:24:00,720
to the immediately forthcoming future,

226
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:02,040
not the distant future.

227
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:04,260
Yet forty days,

228
00:24:04,260 --> 00:24:06,740
and Nineveh will be destroyed.

229
00:24:06,740 --> 00:24:10,640
There will not be dew or rain three years,

230
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:12,620
but according to my word.

231
00:24:12,620 --> 00:24:16,480
John remains within this range,

232
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:19,900
seen in his emphasis on the imminence

